  "notes": "The 1997 template for female pop-rock radio: about 92–100 straight with the backbeat on 2&4 and — the fact that decides the feel — \"a shuffled 16th strum\", which is the only warrant in this batch for moving `swing` off straight. It sits at 0.56, between the subtle modern setting and the classic MPC one. Drums are a live kit with programmed loop reinforcement, so `humanize` opens up while the grid stays close; three deltas are quoted: \"kick 1 and the '&' of 3\", \"snare 2&4 with a tight room sound\" (a modest ghost with a tight velocity band), and \"tambourine and shaker on 16ths in the chorus\", which is the perc block. Harmony is F major running I–V–vi–IV with a suspended IV on the pre-chorus and no modulation, hence the sus substitution and the flat family list. The melody is \"conversational, syncopated against the strum, chorus a stepwise rise to a held note\", which is a mid register, a moderate density and an arch contour, and the bass \"follows the acoustic guitar's harmonic rhythm\" with \"a single octave-drop before the chorus\" — `independent_riff` with the octave as its passing tone. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research says the tempo is inferred and marks it **[LOW-CONF]**: there is no published BPM and the band comes from the \"shuffling acoustic rocker\" description. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are `swing.amount`, all drum probabilities and `bpm.mode` 96.",
